from e import *
E(7,'paper-boats','Paper Boats',
 ('A boat made of paper','When you think of paper boats, what comes to mind? A rainy day, a puddle, a stream? What would someone hope for when they send a paper boat down a stream? Rabindranath Tagore\'s poem is about a child who sends paper boats out into the world and dreams about them at night.'),
 [('Before reading',['You think about what paper boats remind you of and what someone might hope for when floating one down a stream. You also predict what a poem called Paper Boats might be about.','A short passage about a stream near a grandparent\'s house uses words such as running, skipping, bulging sails, lading and burying. Match each to its meaning: running means flowing, skipping means moving lightly and quickly, bulging means swelling outward, lading means loading, and burying means pushing deep into.']),
  ('The poem in brief',['Day after day the child floats paper boats one by one down the running stream. In big black letters on each boat he writes his name and the name of his village.','He hopes that someone in some strange land will find them and know who he is.','He loads the boats with shiuli flowers from his garden, hoping these blooms of the dawn will be carried safely to land in the night.','As he launches them and looks up at the sky, he sees little clouds setting white bulging sails, and he wonders what playmate in the sky sends them down the air to race with his boats.','When night comes he buries his face in his arms and dreams that his paper boats float on and on under the midnight stars. The fairies of sleep are sailing in them, and their baskets full of dreams are the cargo.']),
  ('Understanding the poem',['In the summary the correct words are stream, village, strange, shiuli, night, clouds, float and dreams.','The theme is innocence, imagination and playfulness, which are childlike qualities. The setting is a natural, outdoor environment beside a stream and a garden, under the sky.','The tone is gentle and wishful, and the mood is thoughtful and dreamy.','Repetition of day by day and on and on emphasises the passage of time and the child\'s steady hope. Imagery such as white bulging sails and blooms of the dawn paints a clear picture.']),
  ('Symbols',['The paper boats symbolise the child\'s innocence, dreams, hopes and messages sent out into the world.','The shiuli flowers symbolise purity, beauty and the start of a new day.','The midnight stars stand for the vast universe and the child\'s dreams continuing through the night.','The child writes his name and village on the boats because he wants his message to travel and be known, which shows the wish to connect with a stranger.']),
  ('Imagination and reality',['The poem joins a real act, floating paper boats on a stream, with imagination, such as clouds as playmates racing the boats, and fairies of sleep sailing in them. This mix makes the poem charming.','The fairies of sleep are imagined as gentle beings. Their lading, or cargo, is baskets full of dreams, so the child imagines them carefully carrying dreams.','Alliteration in the poem includes bulging sails and blooms of the dawn, where words begin with the same sound.']),
  ('Language work',['The poet uses of-phrases such as blooms of the dawn and fairies of sleep. You can create more, like wings of the wind, a basket of dreams or a river of stars.','Words for parts of the day: morning words include dawn, daybreak, sunrise, sunup and forenoon, afternoon words include noon, noontime and midday, and evening words include twilight, sunset, sundown and nightfall, with night and night-time for the night.','Opposites: strange and ordinary, dawn and dusk, float and sink, bulging and shrinking, and lading and emptying.','In the listening conversation, a girl, Sai, and her father talk about origami, the art of paper folding, and Sai tries to make a boat. The transcript is for your teacher to read, and you choose the true statements.'])],
 [('Match each symbol: paper boats; shiuli flowers.',[('Think about what each stands for.','Paper boats stand for innocence, dreams and hopes sent out.'),('Next.','Shiuli flowers stand for purity, beauty and a new day.')]),
  ('Make an of-phrase like fairies of sleep.',[('Pick two nouns.','Sparkles and night.'),('Join with of.','Sparkles of the night.')])],
 ('Explain what the child does in Paper Boats and what the poem shows about childhood.',['He floats boats with his name and village written on them.','He loads them with flowers and hopes someone far away will find them.','He imagines clouds racing his boats and fairies sailing in them at night.','The poem shows innocence, imagination and hope.'],['The child sells the paper boats.','The poem is sad and serious.']),
 ['Paper Boats is a poem by Rabindranath Tagore about a child who floats paper boats on a stream.','The boats carry his name, village and shiuli flowers, with the hope that a stranger will find them.','The paper boats symbolise a child\'s innocence, dreams and hopes.','The tone is gentle and wishful and the mood is thoughtful.','Repetition, imagery and alliteration create a dreamy picture.'],
 [('m','Who wrote Paper Boats?','Rabindranath Tagore',[('Natalie Joan','She wrote A Funny Man.'),('Hugh Lofting','He wrote Doctor Dolittle.')],'The poem is by Rabindranath Tagore.'),
  ('m','What does the child write on the boats?','His name and the name of his village',[('A poem','It is his name and village.'),('A wish list','No wish list is mentioned.')],'He writes them in big black letters.'),
  ('t','The child loads his paper boats with shiuli flowers.',True,'The flowers come from his garden.'),
  ('m','What do the paper boats symbolise?','Innocence, dreams and hopes sent into the world',[('Money','There is no mention of wealth.'),('War','The poem is gentle.')],'They carry the child\'s hopes and messages.'),
  ('m','What is the tone of the poem?','Gentle and wishful',[('Angry','There is no anger in the poem.'),('Sad and serious','The poem is dreamy, not gloomy.')],'The tone is gentle and hopeful.'),
  ('m','Who do the fairies of sleep sail in the boats with?','Baskets full of dreams',[('Fruits','The baskets hold dreams.'),('Fish','No fish are mentioned.')],'Their cargo is baskets full of dreams.'),
  ('m','Which word is the opposite of dawn?','Dusk',[('Noon','Noon is midday.'),('Sunrise','Sunrise is the same as dawn.')],'Dawn is the start of day and dusk is the fall of evening.'),
  ('m','What does lading mean?','Loading',[('Sailing','Sailing is moving a boat.'),('Floating','Floating is staying on water.')],'Lading is what a boat carries.'),
  ('s','What do the clouds look like in the poem?',['white bulging sails','sails','boats with sails','bulging sails'],'The little clouds are like white bulging sails.'),
  ('s','Name the flower the child puts in his paper boats.',['shiuli','Shiuli'],'The boats carry shiuli flowers.')],
 keep=['dawn','lading','symbol','imagery'])
